  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incoming mission aquaculture India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This mission aims to showcase the Dutch expertise in the aquaculture sector to Indian companies through workshops, industry visits and knowledge sessions. The mission is also of importance because of the possibility of an EU market ban on Indian shrimp due to the presence of antibiotics in Indian shrimp. Failure to implement effective measures to address this problem could lead to a substantial decline in shrimp exports from India to the EU, potentially resulting in a complete trade stop. Currently, the exposure of the Dutch aquaculture sector to the Indian market is limited and restricted to a few Dutch companies active in the feed industry. The potential of the Indian market is unknown in the Netherlands. The Indian industry is not aware of the Dutch expertise. Organizing the incoming mission will connect the two sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
